light-code-FakeTestAudit Audit a Delphi DUnitX / classic-DUnit test suite for FAKE or WEAK tests - tests that pass without verifying the behavior they claim (zero assertions, Assert.Pass-only, tautologies, setup-only checks, vague error checks, negative tests with no probe). Reports REAL / WEAK / SUSPECT per test, and can PROVE fakeness with a git-safe mutation pass. Runs the light-fake-test-auditor agent.
light-code-CheckOsCompatibility Audit Delphi FMX source for cross-platform compatibility issues - Windows-only units/APIs, hardcoded paths, missing platform conditionals, mobile-incompatible patterns. Runs the light-os-compat agent. Use before targeting Android/iOS/macOS/Linux, or when porting a feature.
light-code-StyleChecker Scan imported / 3rd-party Delphi code for style compliance, common mistakes and dangerous patterns (resource leaks, unsafe casts, missing try/finally). Runs the light-style-checker agent. NOT for our own project code - use /light-code-Review for that.
light-code-Review Full three-stage Delphi code review pipeline (find bugs, counter-analyze+fix, verify+compile).
light-md-DelphiIdiom Fix Delphi vocabulary and writing-clarity issues in Markdown docs - swaps non-Delphi terms for Delphi ones and applies bounded clarity rewrites. Runs the light-md agent. Use on /light-md-DelphiIdiom, "check vocab", "fix vocabulary", "delphi terms", "clean up the md", or after editing *.md files in a Delphi project.
light-code-PostEdit \nVerify the code you just wrote (bug fix or new feature) actually works.\nFor each change, confirm the new code matches the stated intent, didn't break anything observable, didn't miss call sites, and didn't break DFM/FMX bindings. \nRevert anything that doesn't hold up. \nThen run the project's tests (large change) or compile (small change). \n\nUse after implementing a fix or new feature.\nÂ
light-CriticalThinking \nCounter-analyze the review findings already in this conversation, verify every surviving claim against the actual code and docs, drop false positives, then fix ALL the issues that remain — not just the easy ones. \nSome of your suppositions WILL be false — this happens every review.\n\nUse after a review/audit/listing has produced findings and you want them vetted and resolved end-to-end.\n\nÂ
light-md-DriftUpdate Scan project markdown docs (CLAUDE.md, README, docs/*.md) for drift after code changes - flag sections out of sync with the code (class names, paths, settings keys, procedure signatures, architecture claims) and propose concrete edits. Use on /light-md-DriftUpdate, "update md", "refresh claude.md", or "verify docs".
light-Align Drive a relentless one-question-at-a-time design interview before any non-trivial Delphi task - a feature, a refactor, a bug investigation, or a design decision. \nEach question carries your own recommended answer; you skip everything you can answer yourself (recorded in an auto-decided list) and ask the highest-stakes Delphi questions first. \nReaches a shared design concept BEFORE any plan or code, so the AI cannot jump straight to a solution. \n\nAdaptive: ~5 questions for a tiny task, up to ~40 for a major one. \n\nUse when the user says "align first", "interview me", "ask me questions before you build", or starts any non-trivial work.\n---\nÂ
light-md-PruneClaudeMD Prune and tighten a CLAUDE.md (or any agent/skill instruction markdown) - cut bloat and duplication, fix stale/wrong rules, relayer misplaced content, reorder for adherence, without losing load-bearing info. Backs the file up first. Runs the light-ClaudeMD-prune agent.
